As a DevOps Engineer, when an application is not accessible, a server is unreachable, or users report slowness, you need to determine whether the issue is with the network, server, application, DNS, firewall, or load balancer.
Follow this procedure in production. Start with read-only checks before making changes.
Step 1: Check whether the server is healthy
Log in to the server using SSH, if possible.
uptime
top
free -h
df -h

Check whether the server is reachable
ping <server-ip>
check the network route
ip route
